<https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/ExpandedLicensing/listVersionAdded> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Specifies the SPDX License List version in which this ListedLicense or\nListedLicenseException identifier was first added."@en .
<https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Dataset/DatasetPackage> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A Package that contains a dataset."@en .
<https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Core/Specification> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A specification is a detailed description of the design, requirements,\nor features of a product, process, system or regulatory framework."@en .
<https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/FunctionalSafety/assumptionUID> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "An assumptionUID is a unique identifier assigned to an Assumption item."@en .
<https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Software/SbomType/runtime> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Software/SbomType> .
<https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Core/ExternalIdentifierType/spdx2iri> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "[RDF IRI](https://www.w3.org/TR/rdf11-concepts/#section-IRIs) An additional SPDX spec version 2 RDF IRI by which the element may be know. This is for reference only, and cannot be used to link elements together in SPDX spec version 3."@en .
_:Nb1f047c59c1c4585b6dde97db9ad0967 <http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#select> "BASE <https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/>\nSELECT $this WHERE {\n    $this <Core/relationshipType> <Core/RelationshipType/providesSupportFor> .\n    $this <Core/to> ?to .\n    FILTER NOT EXISTS { ?to rdf:type/rdfs:subClassOf* <Core/Artifact> }\n}" .
